4. EDITIONS AND LICENSE KEY

MetaEdit can be installed and used free of charge. The Premium edition
adds the applying step of the studio workflows, further delivery profiles
and command-line automation, as the edition table in Help > License shows.
A 14-day trial is available once per computer.

A Premium license key is personal to one person:

  - A key may be used on up to 3 computers at the same time. You can
    release a computer in Arctisoft Studio Hub to use the license on
    another one. A computer that has not used the license for 45 days is
    released automatically.
  - Sharing, publishing or distributing your license key is prohibited.
  - A license may be passed on only as a whole, using the transfer
    function in Arctisoft Studio Hub. After a transfer you may no longer
    use it.
  - Keys that are misused or obtained by fraud may be deactivated.

A Premium license covers the major version it was sold for and every
update within it.

The computers using a license are recorded solely to apply these limits,
not to track individual user activity.

5. DATA PROCESSING AND PRIVACY

Controller: Arctisoft Studio / Bernd Julian Hagen, Austria,
support@arctisoft-studio.com. The Privacy Policy at
https://arctisoft-studio.com/legal/privacy explains your rights under the
GDPR, retention periods and how to complain to a supervisory authority.

Account and license (when you sign in through Arctisoft Studio Hub):

  - Your account email, your license records and, if you upload one in
    Arctisoft Studio Hub, your profile image.
  - For each computer that uses a license or starts a trial: its name, a
    one-way digest of the Windows installation's identifier, a one-way
    digest of the hardware identifier its firmware reports, and the IP
    address at registration. They apply the limit of three computers and
    one trial per computer (Art. 6(1)(b) and (f) GDPR).

Settings sync (optional, off until you turn it on):

When you turn on sync in Settings while signed in, MetaEdit stores these
preferences with your account (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR): ID3 version and text
encoding, tag-container preservation, artwork conversion, quality, size
and picture type, and the enabled Auto Tag sources.

Connected features (only when you use them):

  - Auto Tag: album and artist, the folder name, track titles, performers
    and track lengths are sent to the Arctisoft metadata catalogue (on
    Supabase, EU) to identify the release. The catalogue is built from
    MusicBrainz and Discogs data released under CC0.
  - Artwork search: the identifier of the release is sent to the Cover Art
    Archive (Internet Archive). Artwork remains copyrighted by its rights
    holders.
  - Lyrics lookup: track title, artist and album are sent to LRCLIB
    (lrclib.net), a community database. Lyrics remain the property of
    their rights holders; see section 9.

Software updates:

The Software can check Arctisoft Studio's public release feed on GitHub
for updates. These requests carry normal network information and the
application's version, never your files.

No audio content, file paths or metadata leave your computer except the
search terms of a connected feature you start. The Software has no
analytics or telemetry. Cloud data and your account can be deleted in
Arctisoft Studio Hub (Account & Security) or by contacting support.
Uninstalling the Software keeps your files and local application data and
does not delete your Arctisoft account.

